{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/169831-help-needed-essence-hunt","id":169831,"title":"Help Needed - Essence Hunt","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-15T09:34:26-07:00","id":169831,"title":"Help Needed - Essence Hunt","content":"So my players taken for them Bear Totem of Light for Dead. He resident mainly in Spirit World in Bears Cemetery, where from ancient times bears, humans and other animals died and being sent by Totem in to stars. The thing is that Bears Cemetery is one big Barren in middle of Shadows Realm mountain range. Packs Totem told them they need to reinforce his domain and get rid of Barren from Cemetery. From corebook of <b>Forsaken </b>I read that Barrens need <b>a lot</b> of Essence sacrificed to negate an effect. So what young werewolves can do to get it? Doing mass murder in the middle of nowhere is a bit weird... Maybe hunting for spirits and taking whole Essence of them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T15:28:10-07:00","id":170157,"title":"","content":"Fixing a Barren is a story worth a whole Chronicle. Why is it a Barren?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T16:54:30-07:00","id":170207,"title":"","content":"Figuring out why it is a barren in the first place is key to fixing it. However, doing something such as the Sacred Hunt for essence is not nearly going to be enough as if that ritual is abused nightly, the local spirits will eventually gang up out of safety and slaughter you all. A rank 1 or 2 spirit is not much by itself, but 50 of them banding together will be nearly instant death.<br /> <br /> As for fixing the barren, once the reason for its creation has been found, the pack should take steps to counteract it. If it is a barren due to the gauntlet thickness, enlisting spirits or other werewolves with control over the gauntlet may help. If the gauntlet is fine, yet the area is dry, then attempting to bring life to the area through the building of resonance can also help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T17:05:41-07:00","id":170211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/169831-help-needed-essence-hunt?p=170207#post170207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Figuring out why it is a barren in the first place is key to fixing it. However, doing something such as the Sacred Hunt for essence is not nearly going to be enough as if that ritual is abused nightly, the local spirits will eventually gang up out of safety and slaughter you all. A rank 1 or 2 spirit is not much by itself, but 50 of them banding together will be nearly instant death.<br /> <br /> As for fixing the barren, once the reason for its creation has been found, the pack should take steps to counteract it. If it is a barren due to the gauntlet thickness, enlisting spirits or other werewolves with control over the gauntlet may help. If the gauntlet is fine, yet the area is dry, then attempting to bring life to the area through the building of resonance can also help.</div> </div> </div> </div>You also might want to keep an eye out for Spiders.<br /> <br /> The Azlu aren't always responsible for Barrens but most of the time, they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T17:09:45-07:00","id":170213,"title":"","content":"As Dessembrae said, the &quot;easiest&quot; way of generating a great amount of essence (over a long period of time) is tending to the material realm in such a way that the essence will be generated naturally. If the players set the material side of the gauntlet up correctly, the barren might eventually dissapear on its own (unless an event happens to again disrupt it, such as an intervening spirit that does not like the new resonance). For a greater chance of success, problematic spirits must be migrated away, and replaced with new spirits that help sustain the new status quo. But those spirits must also be kept from consuming all the ambient essence, as otherwise the area would not restore.<br /> <br /> But as said earlier, the specific approach depends on the reason of it being a Barren.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T19:37:02-07:00","id":170343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/169831-help-needed-essence-hunt?p=170211#post170211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You also might want to keep an eye out for Spiders.<br /> <br /> The Azlu aren't always responsible for Barrens but most of the time, they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I as a storyteller try to shy away from the Azlu as the reason behind barrens as it seems too cliche. Yes, they do strengthen the gauntlet, but if my players always expect an Azlu to be the culprit and be correct, there is no fun in it. I actually had an entire chronicle based around a city that had an odd occurrence going on where the gauntlet kept getting thicker towards a certain area where it eventually became impassable. Naturally, my players suspected Azlu and hunted for them using every trick known to them including tracking, asking spirits in other areas, etc for a whopping 5 game sessions of 8 hours each. As they naturally jumped to conclusions, they failed to realize that it was centered over a graveyard where 1 tombstone looked different than the others as a result of it being the centerpiece of a ritual created by Exarchs. It was designed to create the effect of a barren to reduce the power of the Uratha while he and his fellow Exarchs seized power in the area.<br /> <br /> Long story short, Azlu make good antagonists, but they can be ultra predictable","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T23:29:21-07:00","id":170445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/169831-help-needed-essence-hunt?p=170157#post170157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fixing a Barren is a story worth a whole Chronicle. Why is it a Barren?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was tender by generations of local werebears family, so Ursara were taking near dead or dying animals and people to the Totem so he would take them to stars just after they passing. Long story short, family degraded, and only leaving heir said &quot;f#$% it!&quot; and moved to nearest city. As <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear_(gay_culture)\" target=\"_blank\">Gay Bear</a> medicine doctor he is living life of irresponsibility for 15 years now, as Sun-Chaser. I've got idea that awakening of family Totem will summon him to home. I look for hot wolf on bear action, as you get what mean! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( Of course I mean brutal fight over ancient territory, you perverts... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> Left alone, with no sacrifices and help of Ursara in first place, place were becoming Barren, especially as Spider Host come to take it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/169831-help-needed-essence-hunt?p=170211#post170211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You also might want to keep an eye out for Spiders.<br /> <br /> The Azlu aren't always responsible for Barrens but most of the time, they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was my idea from today. Probably by the 15 years our Ursara isn't near, Azlu take hold of the Bears Cemetery, after centuries of war with werebears. Idea is also tempting as my players need to show Firstborns they earn right to be in Tribe. I have two future Hunters in Darkness that will gladly kill some Hosts and prove they worth to Black Wolf. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The only problem with this idea is that Azlu should left webs in Shadow Realm. LOTS of webs. But character made two times trips to Bear Cemetary Shadow Realm, and saw nothing. Could Spiders Webs being invisible? Or at least hidden under skeletons, and a like?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/169831-help-needed-essence-hunt?p=170213#post170213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Dessembrae said, the &quot;easiest&quot; way of generating a great amount of essence (over a long period of time) is tending to the material realm in such a way that the essence will be generated naturally. If the players set the material side of the gauntlet up correctly, the barren might eventually dissapear on its own (unless an event happens to again disrupt it, such as an intervening spirit that does not like the new resonance). For a greater chance of success, problematic spirits must be migrated away, and replaced with new spirits that help sustain the new status quo. But those spirits must also be kept from consuming all the ambient essence, as otherwise the area would not restore.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that it is animal cemetery inside of nowhere. How PCs will done hundreds, or even thousands of burials to generate Death-Essence in the middle of mountain range?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-16-2014, 02:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T23:59:03-07:00","id":170456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/169831-help-needed-essence-hunt?p=170343#post170343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I as a storyteller try to shy away from the Azlu as the reason behind barrens as it seems too cliche. Yes, they do strengthen the gauntlet, but if my players always expect an Azlu to be the culprit and be correct, there is no fun in it. I actually had an entire chronicle based around a city that had an odd occurrence going on where the gauntlet kept getting thicker towards a certain area where it eventually became impassable. Naturally, my players suspected Azlu and hunted for them using every trick known to them including tracking, asking spirits in other areas, etc for a whopping 5 game sessions of 8 hours each. As they naturally jumped to conclusions, they failed to realize that it was centered over a graveyard where 1 tombstone looked different than the others as a result of it being the centerpiece of a ritual created by Exarchs. It was designed to create the effect of a barren to reduce the power of the Uratha while he and his fellow Exarchs seized power in the area.<br /> <br /> Long story short, Azlu make good antagonists, but they can be ultra predictable</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> God dang it bobby! The one time I don't blame the Awakened for it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 06-16-2014, 03:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T23:35:45-07:00","id":171447,"title":"","content":"Still needed is help:<br /> <br /> 1. If Azlu webs can be invisible to Uratha? If not, how to cover it's influence on Bears Cemetery?<br /> <br /> 2. How Uratha can gather large portions of Essence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T01:50:39-07:00","id":171503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/169831-help-needed-essence-hunt?p=170445#post170445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that it is animal cemetery inside of nowhere. How PCs will done hundreds, or even thousands of burials to generate Death-Essence in the middle of mountain range?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they do not need to bury hundreds or thousands of people to generate death essence.<br /> <br /> For example, they can do symbolic representations of death or things associated with death. This can include spreading rumors that holding a seance in the area will make it more likely to succeed. As people begin to associate the area with the dead again, it will start to generate essence. Although for something like that, very slowly indeed.<br /> <br /> One of the key things with a barren is that it is NOT easy to reverse. The fact that it is out in the middle of nowhere on a mountain is quite natural for a barren since with the lack of anything spiritual living in the area, people will tend to migrate far away from it. The pack should be creative and undoing the effects of a barren could take YEARS depending on how bad it is. Months at the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T02:07:28-07:00","id":171506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/169831-help-needed-essence-hunt?p=171447#post171447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still needed is help:<br /> <br /> 1. If Azlu webs can be invisible to Uratha? If not, how to cover it's influence on Bears Cemetery?<br /> <br /> 2. How Uratha can gather large portions of Essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Azlu spin their webs along the Gauntlet, that usually means in the Hisil (it's less likely to be discovered by prying human eyes). You can basically torch them. This means that they're visible thru the Hisil side of things.<br /> <br /> If you need them to be invisible, make a new aspect for them: Say, something called Transparent Webs.<br /> <br /> 2. Several instances of Sacred Hunt, not to mention the other half a dozen rites that exist which sole purpose is to generate essence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T02:10:27-07:00","id":171507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/169831-help-needed-essence-hunt?p=171503#post171503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, they can do symbolic representations of death or things associated with death. This can include spreading rumors that holding a seance in the area will make it more likely to succeed. As people begin to associate the area with the dead again, it will start to generate essence. Although for something like that, very slowly indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very problematic, as PCs are practically driven out of nearest town by Bale Hounds pack they need to defeat in long term, but now must get stronger after they last confrontation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/169831-help-needed-essence-hunt?p=171503#post171503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the key things with a barren is that it is NOT easy to reverse. The fact that it is out in the middle of nowhere on a mountain is quite natural for a barren since with the lack of anything spiritual living in the area, people will tend to migrate far away from it. The pack should be creative and undoing the effects of a barren could take YEARS depending on how bad it is. Months at the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is that players wanted to make this place they main Locus... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T02:50:50-07:00","id":171521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/169831-help-needed-essence-hunt?p=171506#post171506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Azlu spin their webs along the Gauntlet, that usually means in the Hisil (it's less likely to be discovered by prying human eyes). You can basically torch them. This means that they're visible thru the Hisil side of things.<br /> <br /> If you need them to be invisible, make a new aspect for them: Say, something called Transparent Webs.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Yo Plays-with-matches! Get over here, we got something for you to burn.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh boy, I'm gonna burn the spidey webs!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T03:17:29-07:00","id":171527,"title":